      "proposal": {
        "id": "change.peripherals1979.development_01",
        "category": "foundation",
        "title": "1978–79 external peripherals — programming, prototyping and paper-tape tools 1",
        "reason": "Import 14 distinct commercial identities from research items 39, 60, 114, 116, 120, 134, 137, 147, 184, 185, 188, 197, 199, 200. Describe the native host boundary and assess product and core-standard impacts at 1979-12-31. Dedicated memory and other unrelated accessories explicitly carry no direct impact. Conditional comparisons do not establish qualified adapters, provider adoption or measured sales. Prices and cumulative sales remain editorial evidence, outside foundation and the annual-sales model. See the per-item evidence in data_storytelling/review_evidence/external-peripherals-1979/assessment.json. Revised for explicit product/standard relationships: consolidate descriptions into specification, relocate impact prose, compare canonical implementation boundaries and retain source/qualification limits. Historical documentation cannot establish fictional implementations or measured adoption. Per-record evidence: data_storytelling/review_evidence/external-impact-revision/assessment.json.",
